  "scope_id": "TRIPLE-PRODUCT-20261026-001",
  "title": "A Fitting-height-2 group is #P-hard with bounded homology: the twisted triple product",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "Counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups with H1 = Z/3 into UT3(F4) x| C3, a solvable group of Fitting height 2, is #P-hard: the twisted obstruction is one cubic form whose alternating part Borromean moves steer freely, and an edge gadget turns its kernel count into a Potts partition function. So with bounded homology the easy/hard line is not the Fitting height but pairwise versus three-way twisted obstructions.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
